National Cancer Institute; Cellectis S.A.; Novartis Pharma AG; and Boehringer Ingelheim Biopharmaceuticals GmbH. The company was formerly known as Lion Biotechnologies, Inc. and changed its name to Iovance Biotherapeutics, Inc. in June 2017. Iovance Biotherapeutics, Inc. was incorporated in 2007 and is headquartered in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Frederick G. Vogt Esq., J.D., Ph.D. | Interim CEO, President, General Counsel, Corporate Secretary & Director | Age 51 | Compensation: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 975 people. Revenue per employee of $270K ranks in the below the sector median among Healthcare peers. Stock-based compensation of $63K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Iovance Biotherapeutics, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $3.6B market cap on $264M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1389% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -275% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $336M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Net dilution runs at 8.5% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 23% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (15.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins 153% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Healthcare peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 207% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Growing faster than most Healthcare peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Iovance Biotherapeutics (IOVA) Reaffirmed Guidance And Shared Lifileucel Data, Is It 55% Undervalued?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/pharmaceuticals-biotech/nasdaq-iova/iovance-biotherapeutics/news/iovance-biotherapeutics-iova-reaffirmed-guidance-and-shared","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794503966.761,"origin":"tiingo","sen